# Frontend (Alpine.js)

## Architecture

- `js/app.js` composes modules into one Alpine `app` component via object spread.
- Modules are factories: `createXModule(state)` returning methods that close over shared state.
- `js/api.js` is the only HTTP layer (`API_BASE = '/api'`). Do not call `fetch` from feature modules.
- Shared state lives in `js/state.js` (`createAppState`).

## Entrypoint

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `js/app.js` | Live Alpine composition (loaded by `index.html` as `type="module"`) |
| `js/*.js` | Feature modules — methods must use `this` |
| `app.js` (root) | Legacy monolith — reference only |

Load order: module script first, then Alpine CDN with `defer` (modules run before deferred classic scripts, so `alpine:init` listeners register in time).

## Patterns

- Tab state: `currentTab` (`pos`, `kds`, `recipes`, `tables`, `reports`, inventory UI via flags).
- Forms: `showXForm`, `editingX`, `xForm` object; reset on cancel/save.
- Translations: `translations.*` + `changeLanguage('en'|'ar')`; keep EN/AR keys in sync.
- Persist key data under `restaurant_*` localStorage keys used by `api.localGet`.

## API client

```javascript
await api.getRecipes();
await api.createOrder(payload);
await api.checkConnection(); // health probe — sets connectionStatus
```

- `api.connectionStatus`: `connected` | `offline` | `unavailable` | `unknown`
- localStorage is a **cache for offline mode only** — not the primary store when online
- Field names are normalized in `js/transform.js` (camelCase ↔ snake_case)
- Extend `ApiClient` when adding endpoints; update `transform.js` for new entities

## UI

- Tailwind utility classes; brand colors `primary` (#0f766e) and `secondary` (#f97316).
- Alpine directives in `index.html`; keep markup and state property names aligned.
- Respect RTL (`:dir="direction"`) — avoid hard-coded left/right where logical properties work.
